Backport of teamchong/pxpipe a61aed3 (#250) to evan-choi/pxpipe-go v0.4.20,
which is still pinned to the TypeScript reference at 0.13.2.

When history collapses, the protected opening user turn is demoted to a
tombstone that keeps only a 300-char preview. A long opening task (over
userTextMaxChars = 2000) is exactly the contract the session runs on, so keep
the bounded head+tail form (verbatim up to 4000 chars, else 2600 + 1400)
that the library already uses for the latest collapsed user turn.

Drop this patch when the Go port advances its baseline past a61aed3; it will
stop applying at that point.

